# GoalLatch line-ending policy.
#
# The repository, every checkout on every OS, and every tool that reads the
# working tree must observe the same bytes. CI extracts the crate version with
# `sed` and compares generated JSON Schema artifacts byte-for-byte, so a
# checkout that silently rewrites LF as CRLF turns a valid tree into a failing
# one. Git's `core.autocrlf` is a per-machine preference and cannot be part of a
# cross-platform contract, so the policy lives here instead.
#
# `text=auto` lets Git classify files, and `eol=lf` forces the checkout form on
# Windows as well as Unix. No tracked file in this repository is a binary
# artifact, so the blanket rule is the whole policy.
* text=auto eol=lf
